# Secret hygiene first. `.git` carries every secret that was ever committed and then
# removed; `.env` and `.env.*` carry the ones that were never meant to be committed at
# all. A COPY . . with any of these present bakes them into a layer that ships.
#
# Since wave M1b this service's `.env` would carry ANALYTICS_PSEUDONYM_KEY — the pepper.
# It is the one secret in the estate whose disclosure is not "an attacker can act as us"
# but "the pseudonymisation was never real": with it and a candidate user id, an attacker
# can test whether a person is in the event store. Baking it into an image layer would put
# it in every registry mirror that ever pulled the tag, and a layer cannot be rotated.
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

node_modules
dist
*.tsbuildinfo
.github
README.md
